course: dictionary
lesson: 14825
title: Quirk: odd habits, lucky chances and sudden twists
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A quirk is something strange or unusual. The word can mean three things, and the words around it show you which one. «One of Mia's quirks is wearing odd socks.» Wearing odd socks is a strange habit, so here a quirk is an odd habit.
explain: «By a quirk of fate, the two friends were born on the same day.» Nobody planned this. The words of fate tell you that chance caused it, so here a quirk is a strange thing that happens by chance.
explain: The third meaning is a sudden twist or turn. «Her signature ended with a quick quirk, like a tiny curl.» The word quick and the word curl are clues. Ask yourself: what would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense.
fact: A quirk is a strange or unusual habit, such as «one of her quirks is wearing odd socks».
fact: «A quirk of fate» means a strange thing that happens by chance.
fact: «A quirk of history» means an odd fact from the past that happened by chance.
fact: A quirk can also be a sudden twist or turn, like a quick curl in handwriting.
fact: In stories, quirks make characters memorable and real. «Little quirks» are the small odd habits that everyone has.
exercise: «One of her quirks is wearing odd socks.» What is a quirk here? | A long journey | *A strange or unusual habit | A loud noise | A kind of sock
exercise: «By a quirk of fate, they were born on the same day.» What does quirk of fate mean? | A sad plan made by a teacher | A rule for making friends | *A strange thing that happens by chance | A kind of weather
exercise: Ruby says a quirk is always a bad thing. What is the right meaning? | *Strange or unusual, and not always bad | A loud shout | A storm that breaks trees | A type of school bag
test: «The pen made a quick quirk at the end of her name.» What does quirk mean here? | A kind of ink | A long, straight line | *A sudden twist or turn | A type of pen
test: «A quirk of history explains why the old castle has a secret door.» Which meaning fits best? | *An odd fact from the past that happened by chance | A kind of history book | A rule for building castles | A famous king
exam: Which word is closest in meaning to quirk, as in «little quirks»? | hurry | silence | sunshine | *oddity
